a.description:
I’m Josh — a builder, business owner, and Kiwi dad sharing what it actually takes to build homes in New Zealand.

I dropped out of school at 16 and scrubbed toilets at Macca’s before building my way up through hard lessons, big mistakes, and a relentless drive to do things better.

This channel documents the raw, real side of the construction industry. I don’t pretend to have all the answers, but we don't just show the shiny finished product either. We show the mud, the dodgy sites, the budget blowouts, the team talk, and the problem-solving it takes to get it done.

WHAT WE'RE BUILDING:
// LESSONS FROM REAL BUILDS: The good, the bad, and the ugly of NZ construction.
// TIME LAPSES & SUBDIVISIONS: Watching the hard work pay off from the ground up.
// JOSH'S SITE SMARTS: Real talk, tool tips, and trade advice for builders and DIYers.

Whether you’re running a trade, planning your own build, or just love seeing how things come together—you’re in the right place.
